  "worked_solution": "The Cartesian equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $72$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}12{y}^{2}-8{x}^{2} & =72 \\\\ \\frac{12{y}^{2}}{72}-\\frac{8{x}^{2}}{72} & =\\frac{72}{72} \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{6}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$",
